== définition
num intégré                        num/int
disjoint? num                      
int | string refusé                ERREUR union: alternatives i and s can take the same value, so the value could not tell which one it is; a union must be disjoint. Write a sum with "," to tag the alternatives
double | string refusé             ERREUR union: alternatives d and s can take the same value, so the value could not tell which one it is; a union must be disjoint. Write a sum with "," to tag the alternatives
== lecture : la variante du texte canonique
num 10                             10 num/int
num -3                             -3 num/int
num 0x10                           16 num/int
num 2.0                            2.0 num/double
num 2e1                            20.0 num/double
num 1e300                          1e+300 num/double
num .5                             0.5 num/double
num inf                            Inf num/double
num abc refusé                     ERREUR value "abc" matches no variant of num
num {} refusé                      ERREUR value "" matches no variant of num
union : pas d'étiquette            ERREUR value "d 1.5" matches no variant of num
== expr : sémantique de Tcl
int / 2                            2
double / 2                         2.5
0x10 normalisé                     16
== champs d'un produit
champs int                         3
champs mixtes                      3.5
champ lu nu                        1 2.5
type du champ                      num/int num/double
== listes et boucles
list.num normalisée                1 2.0 16 3.0
lindex typé                        num/int num/double
boucle : éléments nus              {} {}
éléments nus en boucle             0 1.0
somme                              6.5
lappend                            1 2.0 16
lappend refusé                     ERREUR value "x" matches no variant of num
